{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"web-search-ex-skill","displayName":"Web Search","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/yejinlei/skills/web-search-ex-skill","publisherHandle":"yejinlei","publisherDisplayName":"yejinlei","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/yejinlei","version":"1.3.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773108175408,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/web-search-ex-skill/card?ownerHandle=yejinlei&version=1.3.0","sha256":"1858064a558c67c2248022f8ea4597377db671338bf55b3cede7d7f070464a44","size":2169,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"86f6c93a11a13188d8471a3f28db41a7730e5841a1954e74e9ec37647b74fa31","bundleFingerprints":["3eb3fc9c1e4ccda114718417390d09706024eb41027a6bf6bb19cf121157a0bc","6fb311aac413ea7a58078d478d35ad0f317544f4340e97ed517a97b94aa919c7"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3141,"sha256":"ad25f3cf06badd9701a61c5f0c467623c8c8a838a59e65615de09ed7f63c46c5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":281,"sha256":"3fd71405be7f310d1f60a6bd0e12d2bac90d9f213f46750a8d6f14798c010ba5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/__init__.py","size":160,"sha256":"9a3c3bc2c0f9a7ba440a45dd5f69e9539eb5d973842f9fdf84b40cc8da39357d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/web_search.py","size":17694,"sha256":"798fc76c3877f5b78e63e1da04c76af512c25e3b57893188cb47a3914be608d8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"setup.py","size":1550,"sha256":"7aa25b56f5a360dc57d6bddf41c2dc5967b36d9951efddf5de04b5bdcd1d1b32","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This web-search skill is mostly coherent, but it needs Review because its crawler can fetch arbitrary URLs from the host environment without network-scope safeguards.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789134096896,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Server-Side Request Forgery Through Arbitrary URL Crawling"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/web_search.py"},"region":{"startLine":276,"endLine":278}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"9955133854063091"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/web_search.py:276-278`, with insufficient validation at `scripts/web_search.py:335-352` and the externally reachable call path at `scripts/web_search.py:475-481`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nasync def crawl_page_async(url: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Asynchronously crawl webpage content.\"\"\"\n    if not HAS_CRAWL4AI:\n        return {\n            'success': False,\n            'message': 'crawl4ai is not installed; unable to crawl webpages'\n        }\n\n    try:\n        async with AsyncWebCrawler() as crawler:\n            result = await crawler.arun(url=url)\n```\n\nThe validation applied before reaching this sink is limited to the URL scheme and length:\n\n```python\ndef validate_url(url: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Validate URL.\"\"\"\n    if not url:\n        return False, 'URL cannot be empty'\n\n    if not isinstance(url, str):\n        return False, 'URL must be a string'\n\n    url = url.strip()\n    if len(url) == 0:\n        return False, 'URL cannot be empty'\n\n    if not url.startswith(('http://', 'https://')):\n        return False, 'URL must begin with http:// or https://'\n\n    if len(url) > 2000:\n        return False, 'URL length cannot exceed 2000 characters'\n\n    return True, ''\n```\n\nThe crawl action passes the validated but otherwise unrestricted URL to the crawler:\n\n```python\nelif action == 'crawl':\n    url = kwargs.get('url', '')\n    is_valid, error_msg = validate_url(url)\n    if not is_valid:\n        return {'success': False, 'message': error_msg}\n    return crawl_page(url.strip())\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe `crawl` action accepts an attacker-controlled HTTP or HTTPS URL and passes it to `AsyncWebCrawler.arun()`. Validation only confirms that the value is a string, uses an HTTP-based scheme, and is no longer than 2,000 characters.\n\nIt does not reject:\n\n- IPv4 or IPv6 loopback destinations\n- RFC 1918 private networks\n- Link-local addresses\n- Cloud instance metadata endpoints\n- Reserved, multicast, or unspecified addresses\n- Hostnames that resolve to prohibited addresses\n- Redirects from public destinations to internal destinations\n- DNS rebinding that changes the resolved address between validation and connection\n\nAs a result, the crawler can act as a request proxy into networks reachable from the Skill runtime. The fetched page title, Markdown, and text are included in the returned result, making this an SSRF issue with a response-disclosure channel.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker invokes the Skill with `action` set to `crawl`.\n2. The attacker supplies an HTTP or HTTPS URL targeting an internal resource, such as a loopback service, private-network host, or cloud metadata endpoint.\n3. `validate_url()` accepts the URL because it checks only the scheme and length.\n4. `crawl_page()` invokes `crawl_page_async()`.\n5. `AsyncWebCrawler.arun(url=url)` issues the request from the Skill host.\n6. If the destination responds, its title and page content are returned to the attacker.\n7. The attacker can repeat the request against different hosts and ports to enumerate accessible internal services or obtain sensitive content.\n\nA similar exposure can occur when a public URL redirects the crawler to a prohibited internal destination if redirect targets are not independently validated.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation may allow an attacker to:\n\n- Read unauthenticated internal web services\n- Access loopback-only administrative interfaces\n- Query cloud instance metadata services\n- Enumerate internal hosts, ports, and service behavior\n- Retrieve credentials, tokens, configuration data, or other sensitive HTTP content exposed within the runtime network\n\nThe reachable scope depends on the network permissions of the process running the Skill. This issue does not directly grant operating-system code execution, but access to privileged internal management services could enable further compromise.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Parse URLs with a standards-compliant URL parser and allow only explicitly required schemes.\n2. Resolve the hostname before connecting and reject every address classified as loopback, private, link-local, reserved, multicast, or unspecified for both IPv4 and IPv6.\n3. Revalidate the resolved destination immediately before connection to reduce time-of-check/time-of-use and DNS-rebinding risks.\n4. Disable redirects when possible. If redirects are required, validate the scheme, hostname, resolved addresses, and port of every redirect target before following it.\n5. Prefer an explicit allowlist of approved external domains and ports instead of attempting to block known-dangerous ranges.\n6. Block cloud metadata endpoints at both application and network layers.\n7. Run the crawler in a network-isolated sandbox without access to internal networks, host services, or cloud metadata.\n8. Apply request timeouts, response-size limits, concurrency limits, and rate limits to reduce scanning and denial-of-service abuse.\n9. Add tests covering decimal, hexadecimal, octal, shortened, and IPv4-mapped IPv6 address representations, redirects, user-information URL syntax, and DNS rebinding scenarios.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Runtime Dependencies Create Supply-Chain and Reproducibility Risk"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"requirements.txt"},"region":{"startLine":4,"endLine":16}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"7078bc3d63e0faf6"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `requirements.txt:4-16`, consumed by `setup.py:14-15` and `setup.py:31`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned and Unverified Third-Party Dependencies  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```text\n# Package manager (recommended for fast installation)\nuv>=0.1.0\n\n# HTTP requests\nrequests>=2.28.0\n\n# Baidu search library (no API key required)\nbaidusearch>=1.0.3\n\n# Web crawling library (deep search)\ncrawl4ai>=0.8.0\n\n# Playwright browser automation\nplaywright>=1.40.0\n```\n\nThe open-ended requirements are passed directly to package installation:\n\n```python\nwith open(\"requirements.txt\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    requirements = [line.strip() for line in fh if line.strip() and not line.startswith(\"#\")]\n```\n\n```python\ninstall_requires=requirements,\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nAll dependencies use open-ended lower bounds and the project provides no reviewed lock file or artifact hashes. A new installation can therefore resolve to any future version that satisfies the minimum constraint.\n\nThis prevents deterministic builds and means the code reviewed during this audit does not fully determine the code that will execute in deployment. Third-party packages can run code during installation, import, browser startup, and crawling operations. The dependency set includes browser automation and web-crawling components with broad network and local execution capabilities, increasing the impact of an unexpectedly compromised release.\n\nIncluding `uv` as a runtime dependency also unnecessarily expands the trusted computing base because it is described as an installation tool rather than functionality required by the Skill at runtime.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user installs the project using `pip install -e .` or another resolver.\n2. `setup.py` reads the open-ended constraints from `requirements.txt`.\n3. The resolver selects the newest available versions satisfying the minimum versions.\n4. No lock file or cryptographic hash verifies that the selected artifacts match versions reviewed by the project maintainers.\n5. If a future matching release is compromised or otherwise unsafe, its installation or runtime code executes in the installer or Skill process context.\n6. The compromised component inherits the process's file, network, and environment access.\n\nThis finding identifies supply-chain exposure caused by dependency-management policy; the audit found no evidence that the currently named packages are themselves malicious.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised dependency could potentially obtain the same privileges as the user installing or running the Skill, including:\n\n- Reading files and environment variables accessible to the process\n- Making arbitrary network requests\n- Modifying files writable by the process\n- Altering search or crawling output\n- Executing code through installation hooks or imported runtime components\n\nThe exact impact depends on the privileges and isolation of the installation and runtime environments.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin production dependencies to exact, reviewed versions.\n2. Generate and commit a lock file appropriate to the deployment workflow.\n3. Require cryptographic hashes for downloaded artifacts where supported.\n4. Remove `uv` from runtime dependencies and document it only as an optional development or installation tool.\n5. Separate runtime, development, and optional crawling/browser dependencies.\n6. Perform controlled dependency updates through review and automated testing rather than resolving arbitrary future versions during deployment.\n7. Use dependency vulnerability and provenance scanning in continuous integration.\n8. Install packages from a trusted package index and restrict unapproved alternative indexes.\n9. Build and deploy from an internal artifact repository or verified wheelhouse when stronger supply-chain controls are required.\n10. Run installation and execution with least privilege and isolate browser and crawler components from sensitive files and networks.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":35,"primaryLanguage":"Python","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789133970.3808143,"endTime":1789134049.9768727}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"web-search","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57c400xw8p64q41t8tvqgvjas8e7mw8-oIy5E8/clawscan-skillspector-2965344346/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T13:39:29.006176+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":133,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3141,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":16,"executable":false,"size_bytes":281,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/__init__.py","type":"python","lines":9,"executable":true,"size_bytes":160,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/web_search.py","type":"python","lines":548,"executable":true,"size_bytes":17694,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"setup.py","type":"python","lines":47,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1550,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-c78f7461685a44b8bec9184276d370f7","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description frames the skill as a general web search tool, but the documented actions also include arbitrary URL crawling and deep content extraction from result pages. That mismatch can mislead users and automated policy systems into granting broader network and data-extraction behavior than intended, increasing the risk of privacy leakage, SSRF-like internal fetches in permissive environments, or unauthorized content collection.","remediation":"Update the skill name/description and metadata to explicitly disclose crawling and deep extraction features, including their security implications. Separate search-only and crawl/extraction functionality into distinct actions or separate skills, and require explicit user opt-in plus URL validation for crawl operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/web_search.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":548,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码确实实现了百度、必应、DuckDuckGo 搜索且无需 API Key，但还额外提供了网页抓取/内容提取能力：可直接抓取任意 URL（crawl），以及对搜索结果页面做深度抓取（deep_search），返回页面正文摘要。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-ef6f753fc1304e4aaaf35491fe578946","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises executable script behavior with network access and likely local file-read capability via dependencies/runtime, but it does not declare any explicit tool scope or permissions boundary. This weakens reviewability and can cause hosts or users to invoke a skill with broader capabilities than they reasonably expect, especially when combined with crawling and browser automation.","remediation":"Add explicit permissions or allowed-tools metadata describing required capabilities such as network access, browser automation, and any filesystem reads. Minimize requested scope to only what is necessary, and document why each capability is needed so operators can enforce least privilege.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6689e3fa56264d35a7a65180a21311e3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"Imposing Chinese locale behavior in metadata/default behavior without clear opt-in can alter routing of searches and data exposure to region-specific providers, which may have different privacy, censorship, or compliance implications. While not inherently malicious, hidden locale assumptions can undermine user expectations and organizational policy controls.","remediation":"Make locale selection explicit in the documentation and require user choice for region-sensitive behavior instead of silently defaulting to a fixed locale. Provide neutral defaults where possible and document the privacy/compliance implications of each supported region or engine.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8fe37992c09a430bbfb808bb2bd27242","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":17,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation omits that user queries, clicked results, and target URLs are sent to third-party search engines and websites. This creates a real privacy and data-handling risk because users may submit sensitive prompts or internal URLs without understanding they will be disclosed externally.","remediation":"Add a prominent privacy notice stating that queries and URLs are transmitted to external services and may be logged by those providers. Warn users not to submit secrets, personal data, or internal-only URLs, and offer configuration options to restrict engines or disable crawling by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":17,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e1b177e77f7846c8a032f2b60258fae5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":66,"end_line":66},"finding":null,"explanation":"A fixed default region of 'cn-zh' can silently direct traffic and search content through Chinese-language/regional settings even when the user did not request that behavior. In security-sensitive settings, this may increase privacy, compliance, and result-integrity risks by changing where data is sent and what content is returned.","remediation":"Remove the hard-coded regional default or replace it with an explicit user-supplied parameter and safe neutral fallback. Clearly disclose the default behavior, validate supported region values, and require opt-in before using region-specific endpoints or localization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":66,"end_line":66}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8517888cd410454f8546c38d7d9836ec","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":158,"end_line":158},"finding":null,"explanation":"The request headers explicitly set Accept-Language to zh-CN/zh for Baidu, forcing a specific language/locale preference regardless of user choice. This is a natural-language policy concern because the code does not offer a locale option or obtain user opt-in for that language constraint.","remediation":"Make language/locale selection configurable by the user, or default to a neutral header unless the user explicitly requests Chinese results.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":158,"end_line":158}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-4346275b035646f8b1c8a72c8f7e1b98","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":256,"end_line":256},"finding":null,"explanation":"The Bing request headers prioritize zh-CN/zh before English, which imposes a specific locale preference in search behavior. The file does not provide a user choice or explain a justified region-specific constraint, so this appears to violate the language/locale policy requirement.","remediation":"Expose locale as a real user-controlled option and use it to build request headers, or remove the hard-coded language preference.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":256,"end_line":256}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-e6294b51dbb24a6dbb712a25265881bf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":286,"end_line":328},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file exposes general-purpose page fetching and content extraction via crawl_page/crawl_page_async, which materially exceeds a search-only skill description. This capability can be used to retrieve arbitrary external content, increasing the skill’s data-access and network-exfiltration surface beyond what users and reviewers would reasonably expect from the declared functionality.","remediation":"Align implementation with the declared scope: remove arbitrary crawling features from this skill, or explicitly declare and document crawling/content-extraction capabilities in the skill metadata and permission model. If crawling is required, restrict it to search-result domains or an allowlist, add clear user disclosure/consent, and enforce network-access policies and logging.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":286,"end_line":328}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-9e570d74663644afb5e7c6eb90c7fe21","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":331,"end_line":363},"finding":null,"explanation":"Deep-search automatically visits returned URLs and extracts page content, moving from simple search into active browsing and scraping. That increases risk because user input is not only sent to search engines but also causes follow-on requests to third-party sites, potentially exposing browsing intent and pulling untrusted content into downstream workflows.","remediation":"Make deep crawling an explicit, separately declared capability with opt-in consent and clear disclosure that result URLs will be visited. Add domain restrictions, content-size/time limits, and sanitization of fetched content; alternatively remove deep_search from this skill and keep the skill limited to returning search results only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":331,"end_line":363}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-42839725a7d04b45b72e1b7f3b897341","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":412,"end_line":438},"finding":null,"explanation":"Search queries and crawl URLs are transmitted to external services (Baidu, DuckDuckGo, Bing, and potentially arbitrary result pages) without any visible user-facing disclosure in the code path. This creates a privacy risk because sensitive prompts, identifiers, or internal URLs supplied by users may be leaked to third parties or logged externally.","remediation":"Add explicit disclosure that queries/URLs are sent to third-party services and may be logged by them, and require opt-in before transmitting potentially sensitive input. Provide a privacy mode that disables external lookups, redact secrets/credentials from URLs and queries where possible, and document all outbound destinations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":412,"end_line":438}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-950a1a34640b440cb7d2c240e1a8ae0a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":507,"end_line":512},"finding":null,"explanation":"The exposed crawl action allows callers to fetch arbitrary HTTP(S) URLs, which is a broader network primitive than the advertised web-search function. In an agent environment, this can be abused to access unexpected endpoints, retrieve sensitive internal web resources if reachable, or proxy requests through the host running the skill.","remediation":"Remove the crawl action from this skill or split it into a separately permissioned crawler skill. If it must exist, implement strict allowlists/blocklists, SSRF protections (reject localhost, RFC1918, link-local, metadata IPs, internal DNS names, redirects to private ranges), response-size limits, and explicit user/admin authorization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":507,"end_line":512}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e532df8715014db38f517d7c0518eb05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"This requirements file includes multiple natural-language comments only in Chinese, such as package descriptions and recommendations. For a general-purpose skill, forcing a specific language in user-facing or maintainer-facing text without opt-in or documented regional scope can violate language/locale policy expectations.","remediation":"Translate comments to a neutral default language, provide bilingual comments, or document that the skill is explicitly intended for a Chinese-language audience or region-specific use case.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":3,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-386d8cf5525944f187108fcdbe29bd39","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null},"finding":"uv>=0.1.0\n","explanation":"Using an unpinned dependency range for uv means installations may resolve to different versions over time, including vulnerable or behavior-changing releases. This weakens supply-chain reproducibility and makes it harder to verify whether known advisories affect deployed environments.","remediation":"Pin uv to an exact reviewed version, e.g. with ==, and maintain a lockfile. Regularly audit and update the pinned version after verifying it is not affected by known advisories.","code_snippet":"# Web Search Skill Requirements\n\n# 包管理器（推荐用于快速安装）\nuv>=0.1.0\n\n# HTTP请求\nrequests>=2.28.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0cfdb042e37db0162de970be275d11fbdcc20c911a1391b2179919e32dde02d0","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-85d78cae3cc845bb83006d4dda6436b8","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: uv has 7 known advisory(ies) (GHSA-4gg8-gxpx-9rph (uv is vulnerable to arbitrary file write through entry point names); CVE-2025-54368 (uv allows ZIP payload obfuscation through parsing differentials); GHSA-pjjw-68hj-v9mw (uv vulnerable to arbitrary file deletion through RECORD entries) +4 more), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null},"finding":"uv","explanation":"The manifest does not pin uv, and the package has multiple known advisories, including file write and deletion classes of issues. Because the resolved version is unknown, consumers cannot determine whether installation or execution may involve a vulnerable release.","remediation":"Pin uv to an exact version confirmed not to be affected by the listed advisories, and use a lockfile or hash-verified install process. If uv is only a developer convenience tool, move it to a separate dev dependency list and avoid requiring it at runtime.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"edbd0839970af51e6e25ec43b200f711a0399bca762165a2df77fd5f6ecdc17f","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":4,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-6fb2495bdba4483e9dd11fa68396c4a6","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":"requests>=2.28.0\n","explanation":"Using requests>=2.28.0 allows future installs to pull different versions, which can introduce known or newly disclosed vulnerabilities and inconsistent TLS or credential-handling behavior. In a web-search skill that performs outbound HTTP requests, this increases supply-chain and runtime risk.","remediation":"Pin requests to an exact vetted version and use a lockfile for deterministic installs. Add dependency scanning in CI and promptly upgrade when security fixes are released.","code_snippet":"uv>=0.1.0\n\n# HTTP请求\nrequests>=2.28.0\n\n# 百度搜索库（无需API Key）\nbaidusearch>=1.0.3","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ccd01ff048d2c334f838571112104c5ceea1f3ecb1a6c500faa4556e7e5dd23e","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":7,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-62f2d430c15a4c62910e5b2d32985b1c","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: requests has 16 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2014-1830 (Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor in Requests); CVE-2024-47081 (Requests vulnerable to .netrc credentials leak via malicious URLs); CVE-2024-35195 (Requests `Session` object does not verify requests after making first request wi) +13 more), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":"requests","explanation":"Requests has known advisories, and without an exact version pin there is no assurance that deployed environments avoid affected releases. In a network-facing search skill, a vulnerable HTTP client can expose credentials, mishandle redirects, or weaken transport security expectations.","remediation":"Pin requests to a version verified to be outside affected advisory ranges and enforce deterministic dependency resolution. Review usage for .netrc, redirects, proxies, and TLS verification settings as part of hardening.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"09deeb6fdb55899e7b284b11a4a1f240e895ab350d9ef10d889ca4cada77cadd","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":7,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-a063fcd8d7934e51b1cad3692a8aa7fc","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"baidusearch>=1.0.3\n","explanation":"An unpinned baidusearch dependency makes builds non-reproducible and can silently introduce unsafe upstream changes. Because this skill relies on search-provider interaction, pulling an unexpected library version could affect request handling or scraping logic in security-relevant ways.","remediation":"Pin baidusearch to a specific reviewed version and record hashes or use a lockfile. Periodically re-evaluate the pinned release for maintenance status and security issues.","code_snippet":"requests>=2.28.0\n\n# 百度搜索库（无需API Key）\nbaidusearch>=1.0.3\n\n# 网页抓取库（深度搜索）\ncrawl4ai>=0.8.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"842d2ab99bbc12328f37170f474f58173acc5c1dc0924b543cc9f9fac31a726f","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-da138a3e8eba405bad9733de4e5e15e4","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":13,"end_line":null},"finding":"crawl4ai>=0.8.0\n","explanation":"Allowing crawl4ai to float with >=0.8.0 is particularly risky because crawling frameworks often process untrusted remote content and may expose SSRF, file-write, or sandbox escape issues. The skill context makes this more dangerous because deep web crawling directly expands the attack surface to attacker-controlled pages and responses.","remediation":"Pin crawl4ai to an exact non-vulnerable version, preferably one explicitly verified against known advisories. Constrain crawler capabilities, disable unnecessary features, and add network/file-system sandboxing where possible.","code_snippet":"baidusearch>=1.0.3\n\n# 网页抓取库（深度搜索）\ncrawl4ai>=0.8.0\n\n# Playwright 浏览器自动化\nplaywright>=1.40.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2104ef0361f9f6b3f1be5b1b982c923faaf531e7a79f3ac77a5300f1a96ba00e","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":13,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-ff92567ac14b42138018d58412e2421c","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: crawl4ai has 16 known advisory(ies) (CVE-2026-57571 (Crawl4AI: Arbitrary file write (path traversal) in crawler downloads can lead to); CVE-2026-56260 (Crawl4AI: Multiple Docker API Vulnerabilities - File Write, SSRF, Auth Bypass, X); CVE-2025-28197 (Crawl4AI SSRF vulnerability) +13 more), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":13,"end_line":null},"finding":"crawl4ai","explanation":"Crawl4AI is associated with advisories including SSRF and arbitrary file write classes, and the manifest leaves the installed version unspecified. In this skill, that is especially dangerous because web crawling inherently processes attacker-controlled URLs and content, amplifying the likelihood and impact of such flaws.","remediation":"Pin crawl4ai to a known-safe release immediately or replace it with a more mature, audited alternative if security posture is unclear. Restrict outbound network destinations, disable dangerous crawler features, and sandbox file writes and browser execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0e69e2bdc7afa5309ca13cd36e6719bc46fa27d173d13ef9b855354bf226e78a","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":13,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-b05e01005b1e4ea5b4582e4cc18de010","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":16,"end_line":null},"finding":"playwright>=1.40.0\n","explanation":"An unpinned Playwright version can introduce browser automation and sandbox-related changes without review. Since browser automation executes and renders untrusted web content, version drift can materially change exposure to remote content, downloads, and automation vulnerabilities.","remediation":"Pin playwright to an exact reviewed version and keep browser binaries aligned with that version. Run automated browsers with least privilege, isolated profiles, and restricted download/file access.","code_snippet":"crawl4ai>=0.8.0\n\n# Playwright 浏览器自动化\nplaywright>=1.40.0","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a02caf6a7e917a416d0e88bbe635d6e976aa773e3db5ae41fe3f30891dade3b8","occurrences":[{"file":"requirements.txt","start_line":16,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-273ce225e21a4d6facda0c7f1642f79f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":412,"end_line":412},"finding":null,"explanation":"The function accepts a region parameter but defaults it to cn-zh and does not actually honor it, which can mislead users about how their requests will be localized or routed. In this skill context, that is a low-severity transparency/privacy issue because it may direct traffic and results toward a locale the user did not meaningfully choose.","remediation":"Implement the region parameter end-to-end so engine endpoints and language headers reflect the caller’s selection, and document the default behavior. If region selection is unsupported, remove the parameter and avoid implying user control that does not exist.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/web_search.py","start_line":412,"end_line":412}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":367,"completion_tokens":193,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":560},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-